WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.875
This big election just

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:01.835
happened in Taiwan.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.169
China, of course, is freaking out

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.463
because China thinks that Taiwan

00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:06.840
should be theirs.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.299
Some in Taiwan are actually flirting

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.968
with the idea of declaring independence,

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:10.885
And in the middle of all of this,

00:00:10.885 --> 00:00:12.846
the United States has made the decision

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.763
to send

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:14.597
a bunch of American officials to Taiwan,

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:16.766
a bunch of American officials to Taiwan,

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:17.225
which is

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:18.309
the exact thing

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:20.020
they know will just make China

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:20.854
really mad.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:21.896
The United States has to walk

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:22.772
this really weird,

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:23.940
ambiguous line with Taiwan.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.441
On one hand,

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:25.400
they're like required

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.609
to give them weapons

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:27.944
and like by law, saying

00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:29.696
that they will support their security.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.196
But on the other hand,

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.990
they don't actually technically

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.992
recognize Taiwan as a country.

00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:35.869
that everyone's asking is

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.454
 “would the United States intervene

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:38.163
 “would the United States intervene

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:39.748
if China invaded Taiwan?”

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:40.665
No one really knows.

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:41.291
So Biden

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:41.916
sending American officials

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:42.625
sending American officials

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:44.127
to Taiwan right after the election

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:46.129
is just a way of the U.S.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:46.796
kind of saying,

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:49.299
“Hey, we're still here, we support you.”

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:50.091
And in the process,

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:51.551
they're poking China

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.761
and straining

00:00:52.761 --> 00:00:53.553
these relations

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.013
that have started to become

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:55.764
a little bit better.

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:56.806
If you want to better understand

00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:59.142
global politics, follow along for more.

